1
00:00:03,460 --> 00:00:07,870
Every answer from an artificial intelligence travels as light,

2
00:00:07,740 --> 00:00:09,310
through glass fibre.

3
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:15,810
Seven hundred and thirteen subsea cable systems carry that light

4
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:17,330
between continents.

5
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:23,210
Only seven international cables land in Canada.

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:28,170
The United States has eighty five, the United Kingdom fifty five,

7
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:31,850
Singapore forty five, and Japan twenty eight.

8
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:36,770
Alberta has the power lines, the pipelines and the plants.

9
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:41,330
Alberta has no coast, and no subsea cable lands here.

10
00:00:43,190 --> 00:00:47,200
So how does intelligence made in Alberta reach the world?

11
00:00:47,270 --> 00:00:50,640
The route has to be planned across the whole country.

12
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:57,330
The Pan-Canadian Fibre Optics Planner is a map and route solver

13
00:00:57,160 --> 00:00:59,010
for planning that network.

14
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:09,770
The planner draws twenty three layers of public data on one globe.

15
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:13,850
First come the corridors, the highways and the rail lines.

16
00:01:14,910 --> 00:01:17,600
Next come the people and the land.

17
00:01:17,630 --> 00:01:21,320
The planner shows First Nations and Inuit communities,

18
00:01:21,190 --> 00:01:25,240
reserves, land claim areas and Métis Settlements.

19
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:30,550
In the North, the planner maps permafrost, and two hundred and seventy

20
00:01:30,380 --> 00:01:33,990
six remote communities that are off the main power grid.

21
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:39,490
Finally, the planner shows where providers report fibre today,

22
00:01:39,320 --> 00:01:43,090
and which communities have no fibre backbone nearby.

23
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:50,250
On that ground, the planner models fifteen routes.

24
00:01:50,280 --> 00:01:54,290
The southern route follows the Trans-Canada Highway from Victoria

25
00:01:54,120 --> 00:01:54,770
to St.

26
00:01:54,600 --> 00:01:59,330
John's, for seven thousand two hundred and sixty four kilometres.

27
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:03,330
The northern route runs from Prince Rupert to Churchill,

28
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:06,770
with indicative subsea legs to Japan and Ireland.

29
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:13,270
A planner sets the waypoints and the weights.

30
00:02:13,260 --> 00:02:17,590
The solver searches the road and rail network, and returns the least

31
00:02:17,420 --> 00:02:18,790
cost path.

32
00:02:20,300 --> 00:02:24,390
The planner compares three ways from Alberta to the Pacific,

33
00:02:24,220 --> 00:02:29,110
by length, by crossings and by the land each route passes.

34
00:02:30,670 --> 00:02:35,160
Where no road or rail exists, a planner draws a line.

35
00:02:35,230 --> 00:02:38,360
The estimate gives an indicative cost range.

36
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:43,610
The plan is for an integrated Canada, where our natural resources

37
00:02:43,440 --> 00:02:47,210
and capabilities serve communities coast to coast.

38
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:52,910
Alberta can be the world's source for intelligence.

39
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:58,410
Connecting to our partners across Canada and globally provides a

40
00:02:58,240 --> 00:03:02,490
promising future for Alberta innovation to power the world.
